# Merge ownership lanes for upstream updates (see .docs/ownership.md).
#
# A sphere pulls new template versions from the `upstream` remote (the CLI's
# update_sphere_from_upstream). This file declares, per path, who wins a merge
# conflict so updates stay "seamless, light, conflict-free":
#
#   merge=ours   -> on a 3-way CONTENT conflict, keep OUR (the sphere's) version
#                   and discard upstream's hunk. Used for the sphere-owned lane.
#   merge=theirs -> on a 3-way CONTENT conflict, take UPSTREAM's version. Used for
#                   the upstream-owned core modules (odu_base, odu_book): a sphere
#                   MUST NOT edit them (see odu_book Admin Guide), so upstream
#                   always wins and core updates apply seamlessly.
#   (no rule)    -> normal 3-way merge: upstream improvements flow in. Used for
#                   the core contract files a sphere does NOT edit.
#
# The authoritative boundary (also enforced by read-only mounts and the deploy
# gate) is the manifest .odusphere/ownership; these lanes mirror it for git.
#
# IMPORTANT: a `merge=ours` driver only fires on a real 3-way content conflict.
# It does NOT cover files upstream ADDS that the sphere lacks (a clean add), nor
# modify/delete tree conflicts. The CLI update flow handles those residuals.
#
# The `ours`/`theirs` drivers live in .git/config (they cannot be committed);
# the CLI registers them idempotently before every merge.

# --- Sphere-owned lane: keep ours on conflict -----------------------------------
sphere/**                     merge=ours

# --- Upstream-owned core modules: always take upstream --------------------------
# A sphere must NOT edit these (the governance core + the Book). If it does, the
# local change is overwritten on the next update — by design — so core fixes
# always land. See the odu_book Admin Guide ("Upstream updates").
addons/odu_base/**            merge=theirs
addons/odu_book/**            merge=theirs

# Everything else uses the default 3-way merge so upstream changes to the
# contract (ODUSPHERE.md, AGENTS.md, LANG.md), the manifest (.odusphere/) and
# .docs/ flow in. Sphere-added skills under .claude/skills/ never exist
# upstream, so they cannot conflict and need no rule.
#
# NOTE: merge=union is deliberately NOT used for .docs/architecture.md — on a
# structured table it produces duplicate/garbled rows. Sphere modules are
# documented in the separate sphere/docs/architecture.local.md instead.
